# team-compilers A/B — schema-specialized row-frame deformer
#
# Every number below is `read_rows:` from the benchmark process at exit: TSC
# cycles per row for `fp_decode_tuples` over the whole run. The wire format is
# unchanged. Three interleaved rounds per shape, alternating which image runs
# first; the `### AB` delta is the median of all six lines per side, because the
# host's run-to-run spread on this row is +/-2-4%.
#
# build (both sides, from their own tree, under the shared lock):
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker build -q --target dev -t fpq-<team> -f docker/Dockerfile .'
# baseline image: fpq-baseline (main@7e3d2e6)
# change image:   fpq-compilers (team/compilers)
#
# command (one at a time, under the shared lock):
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<rev> fpq-<team> benchmarks.sh 100000'
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<rev> -e SHAPE=mixed fpq-<team> benchmarks.sh 100000'
#
### BASELINE ENV (bench 100000)
### ENV
